and runs about 4.6 % above forecast. For good 0, a missing unit costs 9 in lost margin plus 8 in penalty, so 17 in total. A wasted unit costs only 6 plus storage, so it pays to order somewhat above forecast.\n\n- **Candidate 0** orders good 0 exactly to forecast and good 1 at about 0.9 of forecast. That means regular shortages: about 0.08 of forecast demand for good 0 and about 0.15 for good 1.\n- **Candidate 5** orders good 0 at about 1.3 of forecast and good 1 at about 1.1. That means steady spoilage, a growing surplus of good 1 held for up to 9 days at 0.7 per day, and a real risk of hitting the 244-unit limit around days 9–12.\n- **Candidate 3** orders good 0 at about 1.15 of forecast and good 1 at about 1.0. Its combined shortage, spoilage and storage costs come out lowest.\n\n**3. Under random demand**\n\nUnsold good 0 keeps for one more 2-day cycle, which softens the swings for candidate 3. Candidates 0 and 3 are fairly close on good 0, though, and the daily plans (especially candidate 2) trail by only about 170. That is why I put the chance that candidate 3 is actually best at only about 0.4."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 5017, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2304, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 5017}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-25T18:51:01.088Z", "request_id": "req_011CgPTTJLDkfkCBggvytpTd"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_018k9LApEgvdH9Taimrs4nAy", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {